/P 490 0 R
/E (What we sought to uncover in this issue revolved around this concept. We asked ourselves three questions: how have we been problem-solving in STEM; how effective are these approaches; and how do they connect across disciplines?)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
600 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 490 0 R
/E (The primary objective of most mathematics, engineering and science courses is to solve problems. It is to teach students how to perfect existing solutions and to question the status quo. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
601 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 490 0 R
/E (In this issue, we bring you articles on some of the most innovative applications of this face of science, from how  mathematics has set its limitations and when proof shows us that math may not be the complete problem-solving skill. You will learn about the most recent innovation i aviation which aim to maximize energy recovery in avionic systems. You will be able to explore the same drive for improvement in the search on how pesticides can affect core physiological activities and much more.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
