/E (The greatest mathematical discoveries are sometimes not the construction of new objects. They are the proof that certain objects can never exist. This does not make mathematics smaller. It makes mathematics deeper. Every impossibility proof tells us something fundamental about the world of ideas. It tells us where the universe of mathematics ends, and perhaps that is one of the most beautiful ideas of all: The limits of mathematics are not failures of human imagination; they are discoveries about the structure of reality itself.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [15]
>>
