/E (A piezoelectric ceramic disk sensor was mounted at each test location using 3M VHB removable indoor mounting tape and connected to two lengths of 22 American Wire Gauge \(AWG\) wire by soldering, with joints insulated using heat-shrink tubing and the wire secured to the wing using non-conductive tape. Wire crimps were fitted to the exposed wire ends to allow the sensor complex to be moved between the 50%, 75%, and 100% span locations across trials, and the sensor and wing assembly were gently vibrated after mounting to confirm the connection could withstand impact and vibration without detaching. A mounting attachment compatible with the wind tunnel's holding fixture was affixed to the underside of the winglet using hot glue and allowed to cure for five minutes before testing.)
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [4]
