<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 527 0 R
/E (In contrast to drag, energy production showed a clear and consistent ranking across all three angles of attack, with the 50% placement producing the most energy, followed by the 75% placement, and the 100% placement producing the least. These differences were statistically significant in nearly all pairwise comparisons, confirming that placing the sensor closer to the centre of the wing allowed it to experience stronger airflow-induced motion, making it more effective for electrical energy generation. Overall, the results reveal a trade-off between minimising drag and maximising energy production. If minimising drag is the priority, the 100% placement is the preferable choice, as it consistently behaved similarly to the baseline across all angles tested. If maximising energy production is the goal, the 50% placement is the clearest option, though it increases drag at positive angles of attack. The 75% placement offers a compromise, producing significantly more energy than the 100% placement while causing less drag than the 50% placement.)
/Pg 49 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
