/P 535 0 R
/E (3T3-L1 is a commonly used line of embryonic mouse cells. They are initially in the form of fibroblast cells, a type of connective skin tissue, but 3T3-L1 cells are commonly used in insulin signaling studies due to their ability to differentiate \(see Appendix A\) into adipocytes that express insulin receptors \(American Type Culture Collection, n.d.\); thus, this line is well suited to studying cellular mechanisms for diabetes, obesity, and other relations of the insulin signaling pathway.)
/Pg 57 0 R
/K [7]
>>
