/E (T3T3-L1 cells were initially undifferentiated fibroblast mouse cells that were cultured in T25 adhesion flasks \(see Appendix A\), expanded in T75 adhesion flasks \(see Appendix A\) then seeded into 6-well plates \(see Appendix A\) to undergo a differentiation process to ensure expression of insulin receptors as adipocytes \(Picture 2\). Once differentiation was visually confirmed, at least 3 wells were treated with a 150 uM carbaryl treatment or a 350 uM carbaryl treatment before insulin stimulation, while at least 3 others were treated with only insulin and others received no chemical interference. Samples were accumulated into pellets \(see Appendix A\) and a snap freeze \(see Appendix A\) was performed to preserve cellular activity before a Western blot assay was performed to quantify levels of Akt and p-Akt in each group. Data was analyzed using ImageJ software \(see Appendix A\).)
/Pg 59 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
